      "<p><em>You are keyed up, and you are ready. Those are both true.</em></p>",
      "<p>Neither one cancels the other. You're not waiting to stop feeling this before you go in.</p>",
      "<p>Now forward, and small. Not the whole thing going well \u2014 you don't control most of it, and that's the version we just put down.</p>",
      "<p>The first thirty seconds. Walking in. Where you'll stand. What your hands do. The actual first sentence.</p>",
      "<p>Just the opening. Once you're in it, you'll be in it, and the rest runs on what you already know.</p>",
      "<p>And one thing already true. Not about how it'll go. Something in the room you're standing in now.</p>",
      "<p>Come back. Feet on the floor. Jaw loose.</p>",
      "<p>The state may still be here. It usually is, and it isn't the enemy \u2014 a flat system performs worse than a keyed-up one. What's changed is that it's no longer spending itself on a room you haven't entered.</p>",
      "<p>Recognise. Regulate. Release. Rise.</p>",
      "<p>Go in.</p>"
